WEBVTT

00:00:20.370 --> 00:00:21.630
Are you all right?

00:00:23.920 --> 00:00:25.460
There, there.

00:00:25.460 --> 00:00:29.090
Brother, is this what
they call seasickness?

00:00:29.090 --> 00:00:30.760
Sure is, Kiyotsune.

00:00:30.760 --> 00:00:32.140
You look pathetic, Biwa.

00:00:32.140 --> 00:00:35.140
Sh-Shut u--

00:00:36.720 --> 00:00:38.600
Father, I see it.

00:00:38.600 --> 00:00:40.190
Wow!

00:00:48.320 --> 00:00:53.070
"Itsukushima Shrine"

00:00:49.070 --> 00:00:50.280
It's huge!

00:00:50.280 --> 00:00:53.950
Father, is this the grand torii gate?

00:00:53.950 --> 00:00:55.530
Yes.

00:00:55.530 --> 00:00:57.410
Wealth and might.

00:00:57.410 --> 00:01:03.380
With both of these at our disposal, the
Heike shall attain even greater glory.

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:22.220
THE HEIKE STORY

00:02:44.010 --> 00:02:47.430
Episode 3

00:02:44.310 --> 00:02:47.350
Lord Koremori's dancing
is truly beautiful.

00:02:48.100 --> 00:02:53.190
His performance of the Seigaiha at Emperor
Go-Shirakawa's banquet last year

00:02:53.190 --> 00:02:55.780
was very well received.

00:02:55.780 --> 00:02:57.160
Oh, you are too kind.

00:02:57.160 --> 00:02:59.030
Nevertheless,

00:02:59.030 --> 00:03:04.200
a warrior being praised for beauty
rather than combat is quite concerning.

00:03:07.330 --> 00:03:10.000
Tokitada! Munemori! Shigemori!

00:03:10.000 --> 00:03:13.840
If you have energy for idle chatter,
use it to pray instead!

00:03:13.840 --> 00:03:17.840
Pray that no matter what it takes,
Tokuko bears a child.

00:03:17.840 --> 00:03:19.340
Of course.

00:03:21.680 --> 00:03:24.180
Tokuko.

00:03:24.180 --> 00:03:25.140
I'll be all right.

00:03:25.140 --> 00:03:27.270
This doesn't mean we can
never see each other.

00:03:27.270 --> 00:03:29.810
Until next time. Right?

00:03:38.530 --> 00:03:40.450
Biwa.

00:03:40.450 --> 00:03:41.950
Shigemori.

00:03:41.950 --> 00:03:44.200
Do you feel better now?

00:03:44.200 --> 00:03:45.700
Yep.

00:03:45.700 --> 00:03:47.250
Good to hear.

00:03:49.710 --> 00:03:51.670
Oh, Lord Munemori.

00:03:51.670 --> 00:03:54.420
Oh, no need to bow.

00:03:54.420 --> 00:03:59.430
Though we have different mothers,
you are still my older brother.

00:03:59.430 --> 00:04:00.970
I insist.

00:04:00.970 --> 00:04:04.350
Itsukushima certainly is a fine place.

00:04:04.350 --> 00:04:09.270
Indeed. It is thanks to Tokuko
that we could come here. Still...

00:04:11.310 --> 00:04:17.110
Despite our prayers, I expect it may
be difficult for her to bear a child.

00:04:17.110 --> 00:04:21.990
This marks 6 years at the palace,
and His Majesty is turning 16.

00:04:29.710 --> 00:04:31.960
Biwa.

00:04:31.960 --> 00:04:34.000
Do you still feel sick?

00:04:36.420 --> 00:04:39.220
Munemori's unpleasant.

00:04:40.220 --> 00:04:42.930
Yes.

00:04:42.930 --> 00:04:48.480
Munemori is Uncle's second son,
but he is Lady Tokiko's first son,

00:04:48.480 --> 00:04:53.060
so perhaps Father's presence
bothers him a bit.

00:04:53.060 --> 00:04:57.440
Father made a name as a warrior during
the Heiji and Hougen Rebellions,

00:04:57.440 --> 00:05:01.320
and he is head of the clan,
acknowledged even by Uncle.

00:05:01.320 --> 00:05:04.410
He also has Emperor Go-Shirakawa's trust.

00:05:04.410 --> 00:05:06.450
To the younger brother,

00:05:06.450 --> 00:05:10.120
a serious, capable first son is
like a lump above the eye.

00:05:10.120 --> 00:05:14.540
Then is Koremori a lump
to you, too, Brother?

00:05:14.540 --> 00:05:16.210
Not at all!

00:05:16.210 --> 00:05:18.210
Our brother is beautiful.

00:05:18.210 --> 00:05:22.050
but he's unfortunately a scaredy-cat. See?

00:05:22.050 --> 00:05:24.760
Not much of a warrior.

00:05:25.800 --> 00:05:31.270
Sukemori, with your rotten attitude
and tongue, you're like Munemori.

00:05:31.270 --> 00:05:33.600
Y-You're one to talk!

00:05:33.600 --> 00:05:36.230
You only lack the facial hair.

00:05:36.230 --> 00:05:37.320
What was that?

00:05:37.320 --> 00:05:40.240
Now, now. That's enough, you two.

00:05:40.240 --> 00:05:43.110
How about we go closer to the shore?

00:05:43.110 --> 00:05:46.280
Yes! Into the horizon!

00:05:46.280 --> 00:05:48.870
Well, maybe not that far...

00:05:48.870 --> 00:05:51.410
There you go being a scaredy-cat.

00:05:51.410 --> 00:05:56.000
Wherever we go, we are
men of the Heike, Brother.

00:05:56.000 --> 00:05:57.130
Right.

00:05:57.130 --> 00:05:58.040
Got it?

00:05:58.040 --> 00:05:59.840
Come on! Come on! Let's go!

00:05:59.840 --> 00:06:00.670
Be careful.

00:06:00.670 --> 00:06:01.670
Okay!

00:06:08.890 --> 00:06:12.470
"Itsukushima Shrine"

00:06:22.070 --> 00:06:23.280
Biwa.

00:06:24.950 --> 00:06:26.240
Tokuko!

00:06:27.450 --> 00:06:29.580
How wonderful! You look well!

00:06:29.580 --> 00:06:32.370
Yes, I'm the same as ever.

00:06:32.370 --> 00:06:34.710
You seem the same, too, Biwa.

00:06:36.880 --> 00:06:38.540
Strangely so, even.

00:06:41.380 --> 00:06:44.050
Oh, I heard you visited Itsukushima.

00:06:44.050 --> 00:06:45.760
Yeah, I did!

00:06:45.760 --> 00:06:47.180
I see.

00:06:48.390 --> 00:06:51.850
They even took a boat.
Just who was that trouble for?

00:06:59.610 --> 00:07:01.820
Tokuko...

00:07:01.820 --> 00:07:03.360
I'm all right.

00:07:03.360 --> 00:07:05.280
Don't be worried.

00:07:05.280 --> 00:07:10.240
In fact, it might be better
if I don't have a child.

00:07:10.240 --> 00:07:12.700
I'm sure I'd find it adorable.

00:07:12.700 --> 00:07:13.910
But...

00:07:13.910 --> 00:07:18.000
...the child might be put
through many hardships.

00:07:22.250 --> 00:07:24.300
Lady Tokuko!

00:07:24.300 --> 00:07:26.050
How nice to see you.

00:07:26.050 --> 00:07:27.800
Oh, Sukemori.

00:07:27.800 --> 00:07:29.890
Do you have business with Father?

00:07:29.890 --> 00:07:34.600
Yes, regarding the poetry contest.
But I am leaving now.

00:07:34.600 --> 00:07:38.480
Then, might I take the liberty
of accompanying you back?

00:07:40.230 --> 00:07:44.320
Ah. But in more appropriate attire.

00:07:44.320 --> 00:07:47.860
I shall return shortly.
Please wait a moment.

00:07:57.910 --> 00:07:59.670
You see...

00:07:59.670 --> 00:08:03.630
...Sukemori seems to have feelings
for one of my attendants.

00:08:03.630 --> 00:08:05.170
What?!

00:08:11.800 --> 00:08:14.720
You say Emperor Go-Shirakawa
is visiting again?

00:08:14.720 --> 00:08:17.350
Yes. Perhaps His Majesty has been lonely

00:08:17.350 --> 00:08:22.400
since the passing of his wife
Lady Shigeko last summer.

00:08:22.400 --> 00:08:24.270
True.

00:08:24.270 --> 00:08:25.400
I understand!

00:08:25.400 --> 00:08:28.110
To be apart from the one you love...

00:08:28.110 --> 00:08:31.740
...it is a truly lonely thing!

00:08:42.000 --> 00:08:45.000
Tokuko, I am going out for a bit.

00:08:45.000 --> 00:08:48.260
But I am told your father is coming.

00:08:48.260 --> 00:08:50.050
That is why.

00:08:50.050 --> 00:08:53.350
I do not wish to see Father.

00:08:53.350 --> 00:08:57.810
I see. I shall tell him the
Emperor has other business.

00:08:57.810 --> 00:08:59.520
Please do.

00:09:01.940 --> 00:09:04.190
I am sorry, Tokuko.

00:09:04.190 --> 00:09:07.570
Do not be. Have a safe trip, my lord.

00:09:07.570 --> 00:09:08.780
Thanks.

00:09:15.700 --> 00:09:18.160
Are you sure, Lady Tokuko?

00:09:18.160 --> 00:09:22.250
Surely the Emperor is
going to see Lady Kogo.

00:09:26.630 --> 00:09:31.930
The Emperor has been feeling
stifled over various things.

00:09:31.930 --> 00:09:36.300
It is good that he has a place
where his heart can be comforted.

00:09:38.810 --> 00:09:42.770
In that case, allow <i>me</i>
to entertain His Majesty.

00:09:46.820 --> 00:09:49.280
Oh, is that so, Sukemori?

00:09:49.280 --> 00:09:51.190
You like imayo as well?

00:09:51.190 --> 00:09:54.360
Yes, though not as well as you, my lord.

00:09:54.360 --> 00:09:57.660
You have quite good sense
for a grandson of Kiyomori.

00:09:57.660 --> 00:10:01.500
What a good son Shigemori has!

00:10:01.500 --> 00:10:04.870
Unlike me, with the son I have...

00:10:04.870 --> 00:10:08.500
Oh, how I miss Shigeko.

00:10:08.500 --> 00:10:10.960
My lord, let us sing!

00:10:10.960 --> 00:10:14.260
Yes! Let's sing together!

00:10:14.260 --> 00:10:16.800
♬ What dream comes ♬

00:10:16.800 --> 00:10:19.680
♬ in the slumber brought ♬

00:10:19.680 --> 00:10:24.350
♬ when two souls long
burning with longing ♬

00:10:24.350 --> 00:10:26.730
♬ have a rare union? ♬

00:10:26.730 --> 00:10:32.320
♬ 'Tis of the reality of sliding
into warm embrace. ♬

00:10:34.400 --> 00:10:36.910
Tokuko was here?

00:10:36.910 --> 00:10:41.080
I would have liked to see her,
but I had to be somewhere.

00:10:43.040 --> 00:10:44.960
What's wrong, Shigemori?

00:10:44.960 --> 00:10:49.920
Nothing. I had to go to
Enryakuji over an incident.

00:10:49.920 --> 00:10:53.380
A few days ago, Lord Morotsune
of the Fujiwara,

00:10:53.380 --> 00:10:55.380
who governs Kaga province
with his brother,

00:10:55.380 --> 00:10:59.140
visited a mountain temple and
demanded use of their bath.

00:10:59.140 --> 00:11:03.060
He fought with the monks
because they refused him,

00:11:03.060 --> 00:11:05.060
and of all things,

00:11:05.060 --> 00:11:08.270
he burned the temple.

00:11:08.270 --> 00:11:11.190
That temple was affiliated with Enryakuji,

00:11:11.190 --> 00:11:14.530
so Enryakuji's head priest Meiun
has demanded punishment

00:11:14.530 --> 00:11:18.620
for Lord Morotsune and for his
elder brother Lord Morotaka.

00:11:18.620 --> 00:11:20.620
However, their father...

00:11:20.620 --> 00:11:22.990
...serves Emperor Go-Shirakawa.

00:11:22.990 --> 00:11:28.630
So, Meiun demands that my sons
Morotaka and Morotsune be punished?

00:11:28.630 --> 00:11:30.460
Correct, Lord Saiko.

00:11:30.460 --> 00:11:36.800
My lord, my sons are governing the Kaga
splendidly. Punishment is preposterous.

00:11:36.800 --> 00:11:40.220
A good point.

00:11:40.220 --> 00:11:42.470
Imayo again?

00:11:42.470 --> 00:11:48.100
Well, one of Shigemori's sons said
he wanted to sing them with me.

00:11:48.100 --> 00:11:49.230
You mean Sukemori?

00:11:49.230 --> 00:11:51.150
Apologies, my lord.

00:11:53.230 --> 00:11:57.030
My lord, please spare them punishment.

00:11:57.030 --> 00:11:59.200
But Lord Saiko,

00:11:59.200 --> 00:12:03.740
I doubt Lord Meiun and the Enryakuji
monks will be satisfied with that.

00:12:05.040 --> 00:12:07.000
A good point.

00:12:12.420 --> 00:12:16.130
What?! The monks are
heading to the palace?!

00:12:16.130 --> 00:12:18.970
To burn a temple is an outrageous act!

00:12:18.970 --> 00:12:21.510
Let's take our petition to the court!

00:12:27.520 --> 00:12:29.810
I have just arrived, my lord.

00:12:29.810 --> 00:12:31.810
What took so long?

00:12:31.810 --> 00:12:36.650
Thousands of Enryakuji warrior
monks are heading to the palace!

00:12:36.650 --> 00:12:40.360
Times like this are the whole
point of having you warriors!

00:12:40.360 --> 00:12:45.040
Take command of the soldiers and
protect that palace gates at all costs!

00:12:46.290 --> 00:12:47.580
Yes, my lord.

00:12:57.050 --> 00:13:02.590
Listen well! You need only drive the
monks away! Do not aim for vital spots!

00:13:02.590 --> 00:13:06.510
Also, you absolutely must
not shoot the portable shrines!

00:13:06.510 --> 00:13:08.770
They are divine vessels!

00:13:17.610 --> 00:13:19.190
♬ And so, ♬

00:13:19.190 --> 00:13:21.320
♬ marching behind their shrines, ♬

00:13:21.320 --> 00:13:23.740
♬ the monks sought to enter by the ♬

00:13:23.740 --> 00:13:26.450
♬ well-guarded Taiken Gate
on the east side. ♬

00:13:31.370 --> 00:13:34.460
♬ Violence erupted in an instant. ♬

00:13:34.460 --> 00:13:38.170
♬ The warriors rained down arrows. ♬

00:13:44.970 --> 00:13:49.930
♬ Numerous arrows pierced a portable shrines! ♬

00:13:51.430 --> 00:13:56.230
♬ Priests were slaughtered, ♬

00:13:56.230 --> 00:14:01.240
♬ and many warrior monks were wounded. ♬

00:14:06.870 --> 00:14:11.660
My lord, has the fire at the court last
month caused you inconvenience?

00:14:11.660 --> 00:14:13.790
Well, Shunkan.

00:14:13.790 --> 00:14:16.920
I tell you, it was a truly terrible fire.

00:14:16.920 --> 00:14:21.340
I heard that not just estates at court but
Shigemori's estate too burned down.

00:14:21.340 --> 00:14:23.510
Retribution for the shrine?

00:14:23.510 --> 00:14:27.930
Narichika, your younger sister
is Shigemori's wife, yes?

00:14:27.930 --> 00:14:28.680
Yes.

00:14:28.680 --> 00:14:32.140
And your daughter is Koremori's wife?

00:14:32.140 --> 00:14:33.180
Yes...

00:14:33.180 --> 00:14:36.270
Speaking of Shigemori,
in the shrine incident,

00:14:36.270 --> 00:14:38.690
despite his duty to protect
the imperial court,

00:14:38.690 --> 00:14:43.320
he did not exactly come
down hard on the monks.

00:14:43.320 --> 00:14:47.740
If that weren't enough, both the
political and military power at court

00:14:47.740 --> 00:14:51.120
is in the grip of the Heike.

00:14:51.120 --> 00:14:52.870
A good point.

00:14:52.870 --> 00:14:56.000
As things stand, the blasted
Heike will only grow--

00:14:56.000 --> 00:14:59.170
Which means that in order
to oppose the Heike,

00:14:59.170 --> 00:15:03.010
the only option is to rely on the Genji.

00:15:03.010 --> 00:15:06.130
But the Genji were defeated
in the Heiji Rebellion,

00:15:06.130 --> 00:15:08.390
and the clan head Yoshitomo
has already perished--

00:15:08.390 --> 00:15:10.970
His son is alive.

00:15:13.220 --> 00:15:15.270
Ah, Yoritomo.

00:15:15.270 --> 00:15:17.940
Were you to order it, my lord,

00:15:17.940 --> 00:15:22.320
the Genji and the nobles and clans
with grievances against the Heike

00:15:22.320 --> 00:15:25.070
would surely rise up.

00:15:26.700 --> 00:15:31.120
You think you could defeat them?
The Heike?

00:15:31.120 --> 00:15:34.960
Indeed. Even the most imposing jug,

00:15:34.960 --> 00:15:39.960
for us, is easily toppled.

00:15:39.960 --> 00:15:41.540
An amusing use of metaphor.

00:15:41.540 --> 00:15:44.420
A tepid response, Lord Narichika.

00:15:44.420 --> 00:15:47.590
The Heike's necks must be...

00:15:51.180 --> 00:15:54.720
...cleanly snapped like so.

00:15:54.720 --> 00:15:55.810
My. Well done.

00:15:55.810 --> 00:15:58.600
You understand<i> jugs </i>well.

00:15:59.690 --> 00:16:01.900
What frightful talk.

00:16:03.900 --> 00:16:05.070
What?

00:16:05.070 --> 00:16:08.110
Father has arrested
Lords Shunkan and Saiko?!

00:16:08.110 --> 00:16:08.990
Yes.

00:16:08.990 --> 00:16:14.790
A conspiracy against the Heike was
plotted at Shunkan's villa in Shishigatani.

00:16:14.790 --> 00:16:19.580
One of those present supposedly reported
the matter in secret to Uncle.

00:16:19.580 --> 00:16:20.960
Saiko!

00:16:20.960 --> 00:16:23.630
You ignored your sons' misdeeds,

00:16:23.630 --> 00:16:27.010
and now you beguile His Majesty
and attempt to topple us?

00:16:27.010 --> 00:16:30.010
How dare scum like you defy the Heike!

00:16:30.010 --> 00:16:32.260
Are you, too, not scum?

00:16:32.260 --> 00:16:32.840
What?

00:16:32.840 --> 00:16:35.430
A mere warrior doing
whatever he pleases.

00:16:35.430 --> 00:16:37.270
You promote only your clan.

00:16:37.270 --> 00:16:39.060
You grow conceited, and pompous!

00:16:39.060 --> 00:16:42.440
The world does not belong to the Heike!

00:17:01.250 --> 00:17:07.880
After he confesses his plot,
behead him by the river.

00:17:07.880 --> 00:17:09.510
Father.

00:17:09.510 --> 00:17:14.760
My wife's father, Lord Narichika of
the Fujiwara, is also at Uncle's estate.

00:17:14.760 --> 00:17:17.310
What? Lord Narichika was involved?

00:17:17.310 --> 00:17:18.520
It appears so.

00:17:20.190 --> 00:17:22.350
And what about His Majesty?

00:17:22.350 --> 00:17:26.980
He still seems to be safe, but it appears
Uncle intends to capture him.

00:17:31.240 --> 00:17:32.660
I see.

00:17:32.660 --> 00:17:35.280
Koremori, spread the word.

00:17:35.280 --> 00:17:41.040
"A great crisis has arisen. All who
trust Shigemori are to assemble."

00:17:43.750 --> 00:17:45.590
Shigemori.

00:17:45.590 --> 00:17:48.090
The rest of you are not
to leave the estate.

00:17:49.380 --> 00:17:50.550
You understand?

00:17:56.470 --> 00:17:59.640
Brother, are you trembling?

00:17:59.640 --> 00:18:02.350
Well, Koremori is a scaredy-cat.

00:18:03.440 --> 00:18:07.610
Emperor Go-Shirakawa attempted
to bring down the Heike.

00:18:08.570 --> 00:18:10.530
I am scared.

00:18:11.570 --> 00:18:14.780
The days we lived up to now have ended.

00:18:14.780 --> 00:18:16.530
Things will change.

00:18:16.530 --> 00:18:20.000
Everything... will change.

00:18:24.790 --> 00:18:27.210
Biwa! Biwa!

00:18:53.360 --> 00:18:54.780
Shigemori!

00:18:57.200 --> 00:18:58.740
Biwa.

00:18:58.740 --> 00:19:02.200
Shigemori, come back home with me.

00:19:02.200 --> 00:19:03.750
I can't yet.

00:19:03.750 --> 00:19:05.750
Then I'm going with you!

00:19:05.750 --> 00:19:06.710
You can't.

00:19:06.710 --> 00:19:08.210
Yes I can!

00:19:16.430 --> 00:19:19.600
Do not involve yourself.

00:19:19.600 --> 00:19:22.430
That's what Pa said.

00:19:22.430 --> 00:19:23.730
And then...

00:19:40.490 --> 00:19:43.950
Oh, Shigemori.

00:19:43.950 --> 00:19:49.170
Father, please cease your plan
to seize Emperor Go-Shirakawa.

00:19:50.170 --> 00:19:53.510
I knew you'd say that.

00:19:53.510 --> 00:19:57.840
Your fortune is at its end. I hardly
believe you are in your right mind.

00:19:57.840 --> 00:19:59.010
What?

00:19:59.010 --> 00:20:00.550
Don't be ridiculous!

00:20:00.550 --> 00:20:02.720
Those at Shishigatani are at fault!

00:20:02.720 --> 00:20:06.480
To strike at the Heike,
servants of the court, is heinous!

00:20:06.480 --> 00:20:09.730
But I am told His Majesty was present!

00:20:12.110 --> 00:20:18.030
I shall have His Majesty come to
my estate and have him remain here.

00:20:19.280 --> 00:20:22.580
We must teach everyone a lesson.

00:20:22.580 --> 00:20:26.450
About what happens when
you oppose the Heike.

00:20:26.450 --> 00:20:28.460
I do not wish to die!

00:20:31.960 --> 00:20:33.300
Father,

00:20:33.300 --> 00:20:36.800
I, too, am gathering soldiers.

00:20:36.800 --> 00:20:38.680
Oh, how amus--

00:20:38.680 --> 00:20:41.760
However, those soldiers are being gathered

00:20:41.760 --> 00:20:45.100
to attack <i>you</i>, Father.

00:20:45.100 --> 00:20:46.850
You would attack your own father?!

00:20:46.850 --> 00:20:49.440
I do not wish to do so!

00:20:49.440 --> 00:20:53.150
Our clan owes its prosperity
to His Majesty.

00:20:53.150 --> 00:20:59.530
I believe our obligation to him runs
deeper than the deepest crimson.

00:20:59.530 --> 00:21:04.280
Nevertheless, if I fulfill
my duty to His Majesty,

00:21:04.280 --> 00:21:06.830
I will violate my obligation to my parent.

00:21:08.000 --> 00:21:13.540
My loyalty and my filial piety conflict.
I cannot honor both.

00:21:13.540 --> 00:21:16.760
Such is my dilemma.

00:21:19.170 --> 00:21:23.350
Father, if you wish to leave here,

00:21:23.350 --> 00:21:27.140
then cut my head off first!
